<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51668" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθᾰμαξεύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wear with wheels</i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕτεροι κατημάξευσαν</span> (sic) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάσδε τὰς τρίβους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nech.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				354.2
			</span></i>; <i>crush</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθημάξευσε ταῖς συμφοραῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eun.
					<u>Hist.</u>
					p.240D.
				</span></i>
			: elsewh. in pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθημαξευμένος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γύναιον κ.
				ὑπὸ παντὸς τοῦ προσιόντος</span>, of a <i>common</i>
			prostitute, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				123
			</span></i>: but almost always written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατημ-</span></b> , <i>hackneyed, stale, trite</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιλογίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					10.41
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				11.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθη κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.513
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόχειρον καὶ κ</span>. ib.<i><span class="en">
				426
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ κοινὰ καὶ κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				15.677a
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				1.31
			</span></i> (in marg.), <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				424.13
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				6.91
			</span></i> (ind., [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ λόγος] κατημάξευται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Conon
					46
				</span></i>
			). Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθημαξευμένως</span>
			<i>in a trite way</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.Dion.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				218
			</span></i>.</div>
